From: Carlos Cabrera H. <6750732+ccabrerah@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 27] ggml-sycl: deterministic radix top-k (GGML_SYCL_TOPK_DETERMINISTIC)

GGML_SYCL_TOPK_DETERMINISTIC=1. The radix top-k's final pass claims output slots with work-group atomics, so among
pivot-equal columns (ties) which ones fill the last slots, and the order of all winners, depend on lane timing. The
QSA indexer's block scores tie often (masked blocks), so the selected blocks -- and from there the attention -- could
differ between two runs of the same prompt (measured on this model: identical input, different TOP_K output in layer
27 of a 20K prefill). With the switch the emit walks the row in column tiles through work-group exclusive scans:
winners above the pivot in index order, then the lowest-index pivot-equal columns. The split (multi-group) kernel,
which reserves ranges with global atomics, is bypassed (it only runs for rows of 64K+ columns). Together with patch
26, two cold runs of the same prompt give bit-identical hidden states at every layer and identical greedy text.

